repl_back — implementation plan
================================

status: done (2026-07-09)

references I1..I5 (plans/repl_list). pass-through ("back" => keys
["repl"]); pure sugar — ir.ML:664 defines back id = truncate id ~1.
everything of substance lives in plans/repl_truncate; this plan only
pins the sugar and the one behavioral trap (backing after a FAILED
step).

advertised metadata (the builtin table row)
-------------------------------------------

name          repl_back
description   "Revert the last SUCCESSFUL step (shorthand for
              repl_truncate with idx -1). Only call it after a step
              that succeeded — a FAILED repl_step left the state
              unchanged, so repl_back after a failure would discard
              the last GOOD step. Sub-REPLs forked from the discarded
              state are removed; a pin goes stale."
              (source: mcp_server.py back :351 verbatim, plus the
              truncate side effects.)
inputSchema   {"type": "object",
               "properties": {"repl": {"type": "string"}},
               "required": ["repl"]}
annotations   {"readOnlyHint": false, "idempotentHint": false,
               "destructiveHint": true, "openWorldHint": false}
outputSchema  none.

