assumptions and how to test them
--------------------------------

T1  equivalence with truncate -1, including on the edge: back on a
    0-step repl -> "out of range" error (nothing to revert), same
    message truncate gives.
    test [ml unit]: 2 steps; back -> 1 step; back -> 0 steps; back ->
    error.
T2  the description's trap is real and the reply proves the model
    can recover: step ok, step FAILS, back — the surviving step is
    the FIRST one (the failed step never existed).
    test [ml unit]: step "lemma True"; step garbage (error); back;
    show -> 0 steps (the good step was discarded — exactly why the
    description shouts). this test documents the trap, it does not
    fix it.
T3  full chain.
    test [e2e]: step, back, step alternative — part of the wrong-turn
    loop shared with plans/repl_truncate T6.

