good step that was there. This documents the trap rather than fixing
it, per the plan. T3 (e2e) exercised the wrong-turn loop through the
dedicated shorthand against a live server, sharing the fixture with
repl_truncate T6: step, back, step a different way, repl_text confirms
the new script. No bridge test: repl_back has no async dimension of its
own (it delegates straight to truncate, already covered at that layer).
